      "## Question and decision scope",
      "Start substitute assignment lead time with one bounded case, a named owner, and a written statement of what the reviewer is being asked to decide. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. Give the case a stable identifier before any document is attached. Name the trigger that brought the case into the queue. A sample substitute assignment lead time review checks assignment request, skills matrix, and the surviving value in the placement record. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place.",
      "A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Write the decision in one sentence so the reviewer knows what would count as an answer. Every substitute assignment lead time handoff names the placement lead and the field in the placement record that will confirm the change.",
      "## Population and unit",
      "A reviewer should be able to rebuild substitute assignment lead time from client notice, approval note, and the the placement record record without asking for a private screenshot. Name the repository where sensitive evidence is held. State whether the evidence is confirmed, inferred, or unavailable. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Keep the original document and the working copy in separate states. In this substitute assignment lead time case, the record points to the placement record and names the placement lead as the decision owner. Record the export time beside any value taken from a system.",
      "For substitute assignment lead time, compare assignment request with the destination value rather than relying on a status label.",
      "## Definitions and measures",
      "A standing instruction for substitute assignment lead time needs a limit and an expiry, and the the placement lead should confirm it is still current. Preparation, comparison, and follow-up may sit with the assistant. For substitute assignment lead time, the working file keeps assignment request and skills matrix beside the decision note. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Approval, payment, records disposition, and policy exceptions stay with the named owner. Keep emergency authority narrow and followed by a review note. The substitute assignment lead time record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from skills matrix and client notice.",
      "## Evidence dictionary",
      "The daily substitute assignment lead time pass starts with the oldest item, the unassigned handoff, and the case paused for more than two business days. Check that the owner is actually available before assigning. Assign every unowned case before new work begins. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. Open the day with a queue pass by age, owner, and missing evidence. The substitute assignment lead time case note should show what the placement record held at the time and who reviewed it. A substitute assignment lead time exception keeps approval note attached and routes the question to the placement lead.",
      "## Sampling and collection",
      "The substitute assignment lead time exception record should name the condition, the decision, the releaser, and the time the dependent action resumed. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Keep the failed attempt and the correction in the same history. Do not close a case just because the requester stopped asking. Apply the same substitute assignment lead time test to client notice and to the value that survives in the placement record. If the exception repeats, give it a reason code. In the substitute assignment lead time queue, an item without a next action is treated as an exception.",
      "## Analysis and reporting",
      "If substitute assignment lead time hands work to another team, keep it open until that team acknowledges receipt and the surviving record is confirmed. Record the close reason with the same codes used in the exception queue. Note the next review date before closing. The substitute assignment lead time reviewer records approval note, the owner, and the next action in one place. The substitute assignment lead time close note cites the placement record, the approver, and the time of the final check.",
      "## Limitations",
      "A useful substitute assignment lead time review ends with one testable change, one owner, and a date to measure whether the change moved the result. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. A stable total can hide a growing tail. Check whether the definition changed during the period.",
      "## Review and next action",
      "Keep the substitute assignment lead time record short enough to read during the day and specific enough to survive a later audit. Write the note so a reviewer can reconstruct the decision without a meeting. Make the handoff readable by the next shift and the next auditor. Name the owner and the date beside each decision. Link the evidence to the exact field it supports."
