      "Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. Preserve a conflicting value instead of overwriting the first one. Every overtime billing variance handoff names the placement lead and the field in the placement record that will confirm the change.",
      "## Definitions and measures",
      "When overtime billing variance changes a record in the placement record, the the placement lead approves and the preparer records the action; the two roles stay separate. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. A complete packet is not an approval; the decision needs a person and a timestamp. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. When urgency presses against the limit, pause and route the decision. In this overtime billing variance case, the record points to the placement record and names the placement lead as the decision owner.",
      "Name the backup owner and the coverage window in advance. For overtime billing variance, compare timesheet with the destination value rather than relying on a status label.",
      "## Evidence dictionary",
      "End the overtime billing variance shift with an owner, a next action, and a due time on every open case. Keep the queue view readable on one screen. Compare arrivals and completions, not only the backlog total. For overtime billing variance, the working file keeps timesheet and overtime rule beside the decision note. A handoff is complete only when the receiver acknowledges it. The overtime billing variance record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from overtime rule and invoice.",
      "## Sampling and collection",
      "When the record does not match the surviving value, preserve both versions, record the observation times, and route one answerable question to the the placement lead. Preserve both values and the time each was observed. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. An escalation that ends in silence remains open. The overtime billing variance case note should show what the placement record held at the time and who reviewed it. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. Keep the failed attempt and the correction in the same history. Record who released the dependent action and when.",
      "A overtime billing variance exception keeps approval note attached and routes the question to the placement lead.",
      "## Analysis and reporting",
      "The final overtime billing variance check compares approval note with the surviving value in the placement record; a status label alone is not a close. Compare the destination field, not only the activity log. If the destination is another team, require an acknowledgment. Apply the same overtime billing variance test to invoice and to the value that survives in the placement record. Do not mark complete until the check is repeatable by another reviewer. In the overtime billing variance queue, an item without a next action is treated as an exception.",
      "## Limitations",
      "Report overtime billing variance open cases by age and dependency, not only the total, because a stable total can hide an aging tail. Keep the prior procedure available for comparison. Choose the sample from the export before the meeting. End the review with one change and one measure. Report age and dependency, not only the total count.",
      "## Review and next action",
      "Store sensitive overtime billing variance evidence in the approved repository and keep only the reference and access path in the analysis note. Archive the extract with the study so it can be repeated. Keep the source reference and the coded value in the same row. Keep the note short enough to read with the case."
